  "lineage": "The post-1975 mainstream continuation of Greek laïkó, centred on the Athens pista nightclub circuit and the Minos-EMI and Sony Greece catalogues — codified through Yannis Parios, Antonis Remos, Notis Sfakianakis, Despina Vandi and the songwriters Fivos and Nikos Karvelas, with amplified four-course electric bouzouki riffs over 4/4 tsifteteli and zeibekiko frames at 80-125 BPM, dromos-based melodic writing, string-synth and drum-machine backing, and declamatory ornamented lead vocals sustained across ten-minute live medleys.",
